# Keep the build context small and, more importantly, keep host artefacts out of it.
#
# `node_modules` is the one that matters: it carries `better-sqlite3` compiled for
# whatever libc the workstation runs. Copied into an Alpine image it would either be
# overwritten by the install — wasting a few hundred megabytes of context on every
# build — or, worse, shadow it and fail at runtime with an error about a missing
# shared library.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
# `**/build` is about build output, but it also swallows `docker/build/`, whose
# entrypoint the runtime stage has to copy. Excluded, the image builds right up to
# that `COPY` and then fails on a file that is plainly there on disk.
!docker/build/entrypoint.sh
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report

.git
.github
.gitlab-ci.yml
.idea
.vscode

# Runtime data: the SQLite file, transfers in flight, the gateway keypair.
var
packages/api/data

# The lab is a development tool and has no business in the production image. It
# carries a committed video clip, and without this every build would ship it to the
# daemon for nothing — and would keep doing so as the lab grows.
docker/lab
**/.env.local

docs
*.md
!README.md
